# MARKER REQUIRES CONTENT (markup-carve/carve#513). A bare marker never matched
# here anyway - Sublime applies a pattern to the line WITHOUT its newline, so a
# `\s+` separator has nothing to eat and `-` alone was already prose. What did
# match is a marker followed by whitespace ONLY, which carve-rs also renders as
# a paragraph. Each of the four lines below ends in a space.
#
- 
